   "text": "Boletim PrompTugal, Saturday, 21 November 2026\n\nThe IPMA issued orange warnings for eight areas between 06:00 and 18:00: Aveiro, Braga, Coimbra, Guarda, Porto, Viana do Castelo, Viseu and Vila Real. In Braga, Porto and Viana do Castelo there are also yellow warnings between 18:00 and 21:00 due to heavy showers and thunderstorms. In total, 14 areas have active warnings.\n\nThe highest waves reach 2.6 m on the coast of Figueira da Foz and in Lisboa, with values between 1.7 m and 2.6 m in these areas.\n\nThe fire risk remains low in all 278 municipalities.\n\nThe CISA added five CVEs in the last seven days, namely from Synology, BerriAI, Apache, Vanderbilt and Perforce. The EUVD records 709 new vulnerabilities in the last 24 hours, 33 of which are critical.\n\nData read on 20 November at 18:15 UTC.\nThis is not a warning service: follow IPMA and ANEPC.",
